  "content": {
    "id": "p66-q13-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "13",
    "prompt": "Factorise by equating coefficients, given $x^3+x^2-4x-4=(x+1)(ax^2+bx+c)$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$a=1$, $b=0$, $c=-4$; $(x+1)(x-2)(x+2)$.",
      "worked": "Expand the supplied factorisation:\n$$(x+1)(ax^2+bx+c)=ax^3+(a+b)x^2+(b+c)x+c.$$\nEquating coefficients gives\n$$\\begin{align*}a&=1\\\\a+b&=1\\\\b+c&=-4\\\\c&=-4.\\end{align*}$$\nThus $a=1$, $b=0$ and $c=-4$.\n$$x^3+x^2-4x-4=(x+1)(x^2-4)=(x+1)(x-2)(x+2).$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 55
  },
